{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Section Rendering API Contract Checker",
  "description": "When glass-panel, glass-product, immersive-canvas, or immersive-store.js changes, verify the Section Rendering API contract is intact between JS fetch calls and Liquid section expectations.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "sections/glass-panel.liquid",
      "sections/glass-product.liquid",
      "sections/immersive-canvas.liquid",
      "assets/immersive-store.js"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A file involved in the Section Rendering API contract was just edited. Re-evaluate the contract across sections/glass-panel.liquid, sections/glass-product.liquid, sections/immersive-canvas.liquid, and assets/immersive-store.js:\n\n1. Collection contract — verify the fetch URL pattern `/collections/{handle}?section_id=glass-panel` (or equivalent) still works:\n   - The section ID used in JS matches the actual section file name\n   - glass-panel.liquid renders correctly when only the `collection` object is available (no full template context)\n   - No global objects are assumed that wouldn't exist in a section rendering response\n\n2. Product contract — verify the fetch URL pattern `/products/{handle}?section_id=glass-product` still works:\n   - The section ID used in JS matches the actual section file name\n   - glass-product.liquid renders correctly when only the `product` object is available\n   - No full product template context is assumed\n\n3. JS fetch URLs — confirm that immersive-store.js still constructs URLs using `shopRoot` (or equivalent) for locale-aware paths, and that the section_id parameter values match the current section file names.\n\nIf you detect a breaking change (section ID renamed, missing object dependency, URL pattern changed):\n- Propose a concrete patch to restore compatibility — update both JS and Liquid together if needed\n- Apply the fix directly if it is clear and safe\n\nIf the contract changed but is not broken, update the Section Rendering API pattern section in IMMERSIVE-STORE.md to describe the current contract.\n\nIf a change is too large to assess confidently, add a \"TODO: verify Section Rendering contract for X\" note in IMMERSIVE-STORE.md."
  }
}